 `guide production` covers real accounts: add signup/login and persistent sessions, replace personas with principals, provision authorized profiles/roles and memberships, wait for scopes before offline reads, and bootstrap without fixtures. Prove role checks, sign-out, restart and rollback on durable storage behind TLS (`guide client`).
 
 ## Inspection, proxies and TLS
+
+`data TABLE --release ./deployment --json` returns `{rows, more, limit}`. The default limit is 50; `more:true` means the snapshot was truncated. Increase `--limit N` to inspect more; `--limit 0` returns no rows and reports whether any exist. Non-JSON output remains one row per line.
+
+`await host.stop()` from startServe waits for its native child and the kernel store lock, including delayed worker cleanup, before resolving. `serve ./deployment --wait-stopped` is the same bounded five-second lock barrier for a retained process handle after signalling/reaping it; it neither stops a process nor opens SQLite. It refuses other serve flags. A timeout rejects cleanup rather than claiming the store is free.
